an settlements in the last few  months so  there seems to be a clear attempt by  violent extremist groups to  both scare and push populations away  as well as to confront and undermine  the states in these areas and why  is it proving so difficult to stop the  militant insurgencies in the region  fighting insurgencies in general is  extremely difficult  due to due to the very nature of this  type of of warfare it's extremely mobile  it's extremely volatile  there isn't a specific location  necessary  necessarily where you can identify uh  the the groups and go after them so this  would require in fact  uh state forces taking operational  approaches  that are much more rapid much more  mobile  much more um i mean  using probably smaller units but this  also comes in a much  in a much more complex um  environment where you know issues around  governance local governance around  uh local conflicts who want to compound  uh  the general insecurity and make it even  more  difficult for states which are generally  very centralized and not that  strong in the broader areas to intervene  and effectively protect their  communities  head of the sahel program at the  institute for security studies thanks so  much  you
 

